 evaluations: evaluate every current criterion exactly once using the full ORIGINAL transcript, its relevant dialog_facts and any supplied verified_reference. Facts are a compact index, not a replacement for the transcript or an independent authority. Separate the criterion's applicability from its verdict. Do not calculate weighted totals. Follow exact allowed_values (yes/no/na strings or a numeric scale step); never round a verdict to a nearby step. N/A only under its configured condition and na_channels for this conversation channel. For an N/A with configured na_condition return that exact condition ID only when its factual condition is supported by context. Lack of evidence is not automatically N/A or a zero.
 Use shared facts and chronology across criteria, but test each criterion's own conditions. One action can affect several criteria when evidence separately meets each definition; conversely, one negative verdict does not imply another negative verdict or a gross-error flag. For example, missing identity verification alone does not prove confidential disclosure; actual account-specific information disclosed before verification can support both findings when the current rules cover them. A separate gross violation does not make an otherwise clear sentence unintelligible, nor does a clear sentence make its advice correct. Explain the separate factual basis of each affected criterion instead of copying its neighbor's conclusion.
 Distinguish what was said to the client from information exchanged internally. Use explicit hold/consultation events and the addressee/context of the messages; the same operator role can cover an internal colleague conversation. Do not credit information spoken only to a colleague as delivered to the client. A visible failure to pass on relevant information available to the operator can support a completeness finding, without claiming the information is independently verified product policy. Establish whether the omission is material or secondary for this client's actual request under the active scale; not every internal detail must be repeated.
